1
00:00:00,831 --> 00:00:03,331
And-and I realize that she
stood up by remaining seated,

2
00:00:03,333 --> 00:00:05,663
but now is not that time
to enjoy the irony of that.

3
00:00:05,669 --> 00:00:07,239
(Sheldon:)Now, I ask you again.

4
00:00:07,237 --> 00:00:09,407
(Sheldon:)Who here takes issue
with this person...?

5
00:00:09,406 --> 00:00:11,536
(Woman:)Why should we listen to you?
You cut the line yourself.

6
00:00:11,541 --> 00:00:13,841
(Sheldon:)I most certainly did not.

7
00:00:13,844 --> 00:00:15,614
(Woman:)I saw you.

8
00:00:15,612 --> 00:00:17,942
(Man:)If you're feeling dizzy,

9
00:00:17,948 --> 00:00:20,648
(Man:)it's because the tables
have turned.

10
00:00:22,452 --> 00:00:25,822
(Sheldon:)Excuse me, I paid someone
to wait in line for me,

11
00:00:25,822 --> 00:00:27,492
(Sheldon:)and then
when I arrived,

12
00:00:27,491 --> 00:00:29,291
(Sheldon:)he left, so what you
saw, my good woman,

13
00:00:29,292 --> 00:00:31,822
was “swapsies”,
not “cutsies”.

14
00:00:31,828 --> 00:00:33,158
Oh, no, no, no, no, wait!

15
00:00:33,163 --> 00:00:34,633
(Sheldon:)I ask you all again.
A show of hands.

16
00:00:34,631 --> 00:00:36,501
Who here takes issue...?
Well, stop moving!

17
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:37,470
He's gonna get in!

18
00:00:37,467 --> 00:00:38,737
(Leonard:)Buddy, let it go.
No, I can't.

19
00:00:38,735 --> 00:00:39,865
(Sheldon:)This isn't right.

20
00:00:39,870 --> 00:00:40,940
(Leonard:)You did everything you could.

21
00:00:40,937 --> 00:00:43,507
(Sheldon:)No, I could've done more.

22
00:00:43,507 --> 00:00:46,007
(Leonard:)Now, now, you
denigrated the memory

23
00:00:46,009 --> 00:00:47,679
(Leonard:)of a great civil
rights pioneer.

24
00:00:47,677 --> 00:00:49,107
(Leonard:)That's all anyone could ask.

25
00:00:52,148 --> 00:00:56,148
(Penny:)To be honest, I'm surprised you
cared about the wedding at all.

26
00:00:56,152 --> 00:00:58,082
(Beverly:)I'm still human, Penny.

27
00:00:58,088 --> 00:01:00,058
(Beverly:)Not getting invited
to my own son's wedding

